  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You were built for the trigger. Maybe a corp warframe walked free of its handlers; maybe a Flats veteran who learned that the only law down here is tempo. Either way, you are the crew's front rank - the body between the team and the muzzle flash.</p><p>Your engine is <strong>Adrenaline</strong>: you do not open a fight full. You bank it through the discipline of the trigger and spend it to escalate when the tempo turns your way. Operators are chrome-forward and cast nothing; every edge you have, you bought with steel, wire, and nerve.</p><h3>The Adrenaline Engine</h3><p>Adrenaline is earned by <em>trigger discipline</em>, not rage. You gain Adrenaline from these four triggers:</p><ul><li><strong>Cadence (+2):</strong> At the start of each of your turns in combat, gain 2 Adrenaline.</li><li><strong>First contact (+ your Victories):</strong> On your first turn of each encounter, gain Adrenaline equal to your Victories.</li><li><strong>Called shot (+2):</strong> When you drop an enemy, or land a Tier-1 result on a called or Aided target, gain 2 Adrenaline.</li><li><strong>Fire discipline (+1):</strong> If you began your turn in cover and attacked from it, or took the Defend action last turn, gain 1 Adrenaline.</li></ul><p><strong>Cap by Hero Tier (T5 to T1): 8 / 11 / 14 / 18 / 22.</strong> Unspent Adrenaline is lost at the end of the encounter - you cannot bank it between fights. Signature abilities cost no Adrenaline; heroic abilities spend it. Adrenaline is class power and never bought or fed by nuyen or Body Integrity - chrome makes your abilities better, it never generates Adrenaline.</p><h3>Advancement (internal Level 1-5 = player-facing Tier 5-1)</h3><p>At <strong>Tier 5</strong> (start) you choose your origin subclass and your opening kit of abilities. Every Tier after, you pick a new Adrenaline ability and your characteristics sharpen. The ladder caps at <strong>Tier 1</strong> (internal Level 5) - the apex of a deniable contractor's career.</p>",
      "director": ""
    },
